# Model Schema Conventions

## ModelSchema Structure

Every model file exports a single `ModelSchema` object with these fields:

```typescript
export const myModel: ModelSchema = {
  id: "kebab-case-unique-id",
  name: "Display Name",
  provider: "Provider Company",
  icon: "single-emoji-or-symbol",
  iconColor: "#hex",
  cost: 5,                          // credits per run
  category: "generation",           // generation | editing | upscaling | inpainting
  inputs: [...],                    // PortDef[] — left-side node connectors
  outputs: [...],                   // PortDef[] — right-side node connectors
  parameters: [...],                // ParameterDef[] — sidebar config fields
};
```

## Reuse Common Fields

Always import from `common-fields.ts` before defining inline:

```typescript
import { SEED_PARAM, OUTPUT_FORMAT_PARAM, GUIDANCE_SCALE_PARAM } from "./common-fields";
```

Override defaults via spread: `{ ...GUIDANCE_SCALE_PARAM, widget: { type: "slider", min: 1, max: 20, step: 0.5, default: 4.5 } }`

## Conditional Visibility

Use `visibility` to conditionally show a field:

```typescript
{
  key: "output_quality",
  label: "Output Quality",
  widget: { type: "slider", min: 1, max: 100, step: 1, default: 80 },
  visibility: { dependsOn: "output_format", values: ["jpeg", "webp"] },
}
```

## Registration

After creating a model file, add it to `src/models/registry.ts`:

```typescript
import { myModel } from "./my-model";
export const MODEL_REGISTRY: ModelSchema[] = [...existing, myModel];
```

## Widget Types Available

slider, dropdown, checkbox, seed, text (with multiline), number, lora_picker, image_upload, color
